<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wenceslaus III Adam, Duke of Cieszyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a>–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wenceslaus III Adam was a Piast Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Cieszyn</a> who succeeded as a child in 1528 and ruled in person from 1545. He introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> into the duchy and issued a church ordinance for it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a> remained strong in Cieszyn Silesia despite the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> pressed after the Piast line ended in 1653.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-iii-adam-duke-of-cieszyn.jpg" alt="Wenceslaus III Adam, Duke of Cieszyn" width="269" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jakob Seisenegger (?) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waclaw_Adam_face.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
